 system handler not supplied.

CCL.SV, SET.SV, MONITOR -
	o not compatable with previous versions of OS78/OS278.
	o Any attempt to mix OS278 utilities with OS78 utilities
	  will corrupt your disk.

SETUP.SV -
	o For DECmate II only.  This invokes setup mode.

WPFLOP -
	o Has many fixes over the 3.0 version.

LPTS.HN -
	o This handler now accepts SET LPT WIDTH commandNOTES:

    This system has been built from the ground up, and NO DSN patches
  are to be installed.  All patches have been installed at source code level.

    All the files on this disk have been modified, and are no longer
  compatable with other versions of OS78.  Mixing OS278 files with OS78
  files can effect the operation of the system, or destroy the system disk
  and or the data disk.  Use HELP to operate the OS278 system.

    Documentation is never perfect or complete.  Trying to document a system
  without writing a manual isn't easy.  However the documentation supplied
  should help in using most of the enhancements.  If you do need a manual
  refer to OS/78 User's Manual (order # AA-5748C-TA).

    This system version is 1.0.

	1 = Version of current system build

		On version change all files have the same date.

	0 = Edit history of files on this system.

		On edit change only the files effected will have a new date.


						Good luck, and Good Coding

							T.A.D.
	The
	Anonymous
	Developer

  This software is not supported.  DIGITAL is not responsible for the
  accuracy and or reliablitiy of this software on any equipment.

Some quick notes on major changes:

MONTIOR -
	o Can accept LC input

DUPLICATE - 
	o Not compatable with OS278.  (File RXCOPY.SV has been removed)
	o All formatting is now done by FORMAT.SV.

RX01/02 -
	o Device names have changed from RXA0-3 to RX20-3.
	o The new RX handlers not compatable with original RX handlers.
	o RX01.
	o Modifications have been made to pass 7 bit characters,
	  and all control codes.

FUTIL, BATCH -
	o Has been modified to allow patching under BATCH control.
	o Batch, system commands must be in upper case.

CREF.SV -
	o The CREF literal table has been fixed.

HELP.HL -
	o The help file reflects the changes made to this system.

BASIC system -
	o Refer to the BASIC.CM file for the enhancements.

RENUM.BA -
	o Replaces RESEQ.BA, requires this system for operation.
	  List out the file for operation procedures.

EDIT.SV -
	o Virtual text editor.  Refer to EDTHLP.TX file.
